 "topics": [
  {
   "topic": "Whether an import-time Registry 404 creates a rejected SnapshotImportRecord or no record",
   "members": [
    "r1.00",
    "r2.00",
    "r3.00"
   ],
   "runs": [
    1,
    2,
    3
   ],
   "questions": [
    "When the project passed the route check but Registry returns HTTP 404 during the import, does the portal create a rejected SnapshotImportRecord or record nothing?",
    "When the import-time Registry request returns HTTP 404 for the project after the route previously validated it as active, is that a not-existing project rejection that creates a SnapshotImportRecord, or a Registry failure that creates no record?",
    "When the route check succeeds but the import's Registry call returns HTTP 404, is a rejected SnapshotImportRecord created or is the request failed with no record?"
   ],
   "units": [
    "context"
   ],
   "witnessed_by": [
    "r1.00",
    "r2.00",
    "r3.00"
   ],
   "id": "T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "answered",
    "quotes": [
     "A project that the Registry answers as not existing or not active, or that loses its grant, or a capability refused, between the route's check and the import is recorded as a rejection for that reason; a principal disabled in between, or a storage or Registry failure during the import (an HTTP 404 from the Registry among them, R6), is answered as that failure and records nothing."
    ],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "The text distinguishes a decoded Registry answer that the project does not exist from an HTTP 404 transport/boundary failure and explicitly says the latter records nothing.",
